! STEP 1: the working slab + exactly ONE fold (TIR @D, the top flat edge).
! Isolates the REFLECTION convention. S2 (entry) is unchanged from diag_slab (it traced).
! We expect: beam enters at A (up-right), hits the D mirror, reflects DOWN-right, reaches image.
LEN NEW
DIM M
WL 587.56
REF 1
EPD 8.000000
YAN 23.884815
PRV
PWL 587.56
'FOLDN' 1.500000
END
SO 0 1e18
YDE S1 9.459225
STO S1
THI S1 37.207328
! S2: A entry (refract into glass) -- SAME as the slab, but THI shortened to reach D (11.84 mm)
S 156.054833 11.844593 'FOLDN'
ADE S2 10.876174
! S3: D fold -- flat top edge, TIR (stay in glass). ADE puts the mirror normal ~horizontal
!     in the frame S2 propagated (local +Z is at 10.876 deg; D normal wants engine +Y=90 deg).
!     Reflected space -> THI is NEGATIVE.
S 0 -25.0 TIRO 'FOLDN'
ADE S3 79.123826
! image just after the fold, so we can SEE the reflected beam direction
SI 0 0
CIR SI 20.0
GO
